.TH VANTOOL 1 "October 2026" "vantool" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vantool \- inspect, build, cut, convert and repair VistaPro .VAN animations
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vantool info
.I FILE.VAN
.br
.B vantool extract
.I FILE.VAN PREFIX
.RB [ \-t
.IR bmp | pcx ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR FIRST ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR COUNT ]
.br
.B vantool make
.I OUT.VAN
.RB [ \-m
.IR MODE ]
.RB [ \-pc ]
.RB [ \-k ]
.I IMAGE...
.br
.B vantool make
.I OUT.VAN
.RB [ \-m
.IR MODE ]
.RB [ \-pc ]
.RB [ \-k ]
.B \-p
.I PATTERN
.B \-n
.I COUNT
.RB [ \-s
.IR START ]
.br
.B vantool slice
.I IN.VAN OUT.VAN FIRST
.RI [ COUNT ]
.br
.B vantool flc
.I IN.VAN OUT.FLC
.RB [ \-r
.IR FPS ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR FIRST ]
.RB [ \-n
.IR COUNT ]
.br
.B vantool repair
.I FILE.VAN
.RB [ \-pc ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vantool
works on the VANIM (.VAN) animation files made by VistaPro 3.20 for DOS.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B info
Print the file's video mode, frame count and other details.
.TP
.B extract
Write each frame as
.IR PREFIX nnnn .BMP
or
.IR PREFIX nnnn .PCX.
.TP
.B make
Build a .VAN file from 8-bit BMP or PCX frames, given either as a list of
images or as a printf-style
.I PATTERN
such as
.BR FR%04d.PCX .
.TP
.B slice
Copy
.I COUNT
frames starting at frame
.I FIRST
into a new file.
Without
.I COUNT
the rest of the file is copied.
.TP
.B flc
Convert to an FLC animation.
An output name ending in
.B .FLI
writes the older FLI format instead, which only supports 320x200.
.TP
.B repair
Rewrite the file's magic number in place.
This fixes VistaPro's "continue" on a VANIMPC file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-t " bmp" | pcx
Image format for
.BR extract .
.TP
.BI \-f " FIRST"
First frame to use.
.TP
.BI \-n " COUNT"
Number of frames to use.
With
.B make \-p
it is the number of frames to read.
.TP
.BI \-m " MODE"
Video mode for
.BR make ,
for example
.B 0x13
or
.BR 0x101 .
The default is chosen from the image size.
.TP
.B \-pc
Write VANIMPC (top-down) instead of VANIMWN, the VistaPro 3.20 default.
With
.B repair
it sets the magic to VANIMPC.
.TP
.B \-k
Keep going if a frame's palette differs, using the first frame's palette.
.TP
.BI \-p " PATTERN"
Printf-style frame name pattern for
.BR make .
.TP
.BI \-s " START"
First number to substitute into
.IR PATTERN .
.TP
.BI \-r " FPS"
Playback speed for
.BR flc ,
in frames per second.
The default is 10.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vanplay (1)
.PP
Project page and file format notes:
.UR https://github.com/stuaxo/vantool
.UE
